on to change this unless we find an absolutely ideal icon for it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5073166672/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5074152681","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121675#issuecomment-5074152681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121675","id":5074152681,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLnFs6Q","user":{"login":"Jesusemora","id":32273722,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjczNzIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32273722?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora","html_url":"https://github.com/Jesusemora","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-24T20:35:18Z","updated_at":"2026-07-24T20:43:06Z","body":"The icon is supposed to look like a tactile surface. 3 lines is very common is most electronics, cars, and everything that needs to slide up and down. I've also seen parallel \"arrows\" representing which direction it turns on.\r\n\r\nwith a quick search from google I found this image showing different icons:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"736\" height=\"552\" alt=\"c4d81b3758eef90f1d529d7b2d0c3b7b\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1ce0fca8-9303-4640-8e96-c1ca12398a5f\" />\r\n\r\n-----\r\n\r\n> uses DragHandle as icon instead for the draggable elements\r\n> <img alt=\"Screenshot_20260723_121546\" width=\"262\" height=\"255\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/158825920/625634697-415bc577-f9ad-49bd-8a03-96c5a9da1596.webp?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..RTnlQiq2JvMEcfop6-36IDCxamxd4rtYMIFXA_2cAGI\">\r\n\r\nI think the problem with this is that the circles are **too far apart** and looks like dice. It needs more circles. Alternatively, these would work better as squares.\r\nBut they need to be **evenly spaced to look like a texture**.\r\nThere's also the problem of contrast with the theme, since there's no defined background, we can't expect this to work with all themes the same way. It's also not perfectly aligned with the elements on the right.\r\nIt probably needs a background to delimitate the draggable area. here's another picture:\r\n<img width=\"1440\" height=\"850\" alt=\"65ef0e429d4bf184f42ceb7f_DD_Overview_Drag-in-range\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cbae3c54-dea6-4bb2-9d52-4a4119bbc8ee\" />\r\n\r\nWithout the 3 lines, we need a background for the icon and also a different background for the element.\r\n\r\nThese are from krita:\r\n<img width=\"90\" height=\"66\" alt=\"Captura desde 2026-07-24 17-41-43\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/490155b3-d36d-4d00-aa0b-a6abf34b5608\" />\r\n<img width=\"84\" height=\"108\" alt=\"Captura desde 2026-07-24 17-41-49\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aac13967-eb6c-47b9-b019-b74f56cd6624\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5074152681/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_v